                "text": "**Analyzing the Pattern**\n\nI've zeroed in on the first example. The \"8\" sits at coordinate (4, 4), and now I'm charting how the \"5\"s are positioned in relation to that anchor. Row by row, I'm noting specific column placements for the \"5\"s to unveil the underlying rule. I see a stepped progression starting from that point.\n\n\n**Unveiling the Structure**\n\nThe staircase pattern's directionality is key! Downward steps move left; upward, right. I'm building on the discovery of stepping out from the \"8\" in both directions, observing how each row's \"5\" placements define the staircase's shape. Row by row, I'm working to consolidate the directional movement with row and column dependencies. Example 2's edge case confirms the importance of column limits in stepping out.\n\n\n",
