                "text": "An analysis of the examples shows the following transformation:\n1. Locate the `8` in the grid.\n2. Draw a winding path of `5`s stepping upwards and to the right, and downwards and to the left:\n   - **Upwards**:\n     - 1 step up at current column $c$: $(r-1, c)$\n     - Horizontal segment of length 3 extending right: $(r-2, c), (r-2, c+1), (r-2, c+2)$\n     - Update $c \\leftarrow c+2$ and repeat until the top boundary of the grid.\n   - **Downwards**:\n     - 1 step down at current column $c$: $(r+1, c)$\n     - Horizontal segment of length 3 extending left: $(r+2, c), (r+2, c-1), (r+2, c-2)$\n     - Update $c \\leftarrow c-2$ and repeat until the bottom boundary of the grid.\n3. Keep cells within bounds and retain the background color elsewhere.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid!",
